{
  "id": "./",
  "name": "IStructE - Golden Data Specification",
  "short_name": "Golden Data Spec",
  "description": "\nThe Golden Data Specification (GDS) is a standardized definition of high-quality, authoritative data used across systems, projects, and stakeholders within an organization. It establishes a single source of truth by clearly defining the structure, format, semantics, and governance rules for critical data assets.\n\nBy aligning teams around a consistent specification, the GDS ensures data is accurate, complete, and interoperable, reducing duplication, ambiguity, and integration issues. It typically includes agreed schemas, naming conventions, validation rules, metadata, and lifecycle requirements, enabling reliable data exchange and supporting analytics, automation, and decision-making.\n\nUltimately, the Golden Data Specification underpins robust digital workflows, improves data governance, and drives consistency across platforms, ensuring that all users are working from the same trusted dataset.\n",
  "start_url": "./",
  "scope": "./",
